  "body_html": "<h1>Shapley Value Lies In The Core Of A Convex Game</h1>\n<p><strong>Theorem.</strong> If a TU game is convex, then its Shapley value belongs to the\ncore.</p>\n<p>Convexity means marginal contributions are increasing with coalition size.\nThis increasing-marginal-returns property makes the Shapley average satisfy\nevery coalitional rationality inequality:\n$$\n  \\sum_{i \\in S}\\operatorname{Sh}_i(v) \\ge v(S)\n  \\quad\\text{for every } S \\subseteq N.\n$$\nTogether with Shapley efficiency, this places the Shapley payoff vector in\nthe core.</p>\n<h2>Lean Status</h2>\n<p>The theorem statement exists as <code>CoalitionalGame.IsConvex.shapley_in_core</code>\nand currently has a documented proof gap.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MSZ Ch.18, Thm 18.32] Maschler, Solan, Zamir, <em>Game Theory</em>,\n  <code>references/GameTheory.pdf</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
